_action\":{\"ref\":\"d25\"},\"ref\":\"d25\",\"snippet\":\" ... Later renamed after Greene, the fort was a star-shaped earthwork that mounted six 18-pound cannons, and was the largest on Long Island. After the American defeat in the Battle of Long Island, George Washington withdrew his troops from the Fort under the cover of darkness, a ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Greene,_Brooklyn\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d26\"},\"ref\":\"d26\",\"snippet\":\" ... Health care\\n\\nTwo hospitals are located within Evanston's city limits:\\n\\n*Evanston Hospital, part of NorthShore University HealthSystem\\n*Ascension Saint Francis Hospital Evanston, part of Ascension\\n\\nNotable people\\n\\nUniversity relations\\n\\nA perennial debate in Evanston is the issue of Northwestern University's status as a tax-exempt institution ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evanston,_Illinois\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d27\"},\"ref\":\"d27\",\"snippet\":\" ... It is a part of the Center for Molecular Medicine and Infectious Diseases and is located adjacent to the veterinary teaching hospital. It houses college faculty specializing in immunology, infectious diseases, autoimmunity, and regenerative medicine.\\n\\nInstitute For Society, Culture And Environment (built 1914, 5,539 GSF, 230 Grove ... \",\"title\":\"https://history.unirel.vt.edu/physical_plant/campus_buildings.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d28\"},\"ref\":\"d28\",\"snippet\":\" ... Lists of births at particular hospitals also appear regularly. Some of the hospitals include: Methodist Episcopal, Shore Road, Norwegian Hospital, United Israel-Zion, and Borough Park Maternity Hospital, to name a few. Many photographs appear in the paper, covering sporting events, fashion, and social gatherings. Advertisements appear throughout ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.bklynlibrary.org/brooklyncollection/about-brooklyn-newsstand\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"c2271522e40ed9016a78f20035945fcd90cdb2d5c348c1f5f4dcc6a63fccc13f\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"b20b701afe1354c1b3d3efee4cb090d4214977ded57cee768a4f33e588674783\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"hospital renamed 539 days after birth\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d29\"},\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Boy in the Field by Margot Livesey\\n\\nLivesey's latest novel opens with three siblings finding a dead body. Wearing matching school uniforms, they move together through the scene almost as if they were protagonists of an early children's adventure novel. These are not, however, parentless ... \",\"title\":\"https://electricliterature.com/7-books-that-expand-the-conversation-about-adoption/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d30\"},\"ref\":\"d30\",\"snippet\":\" ... embracing, and wonderful\\\", unlike Eugenides' first novel. Mark Lawson of The Guardian praised Middlesex for having the same unique qualities as The Virgin Suicides, commenting that Middlesex had \\\"an ability to describe the horrible in a comic voice, an unusual form of narration and an eye for bizarre ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Middlesex_(novel)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... searching for new baby names beginning with \\\"H\\\" for each successive child.Behrend, Auguste. \\\"My daughter Magda Goebbels\\\", Schwaebische Illustrierte, 26 April 1952.\\n\\nChildren\\n\\nHarald\\n\\nMagda and Günther Quandt were married on 4 January 1921, and her first child, Harald Quandt, was born on 1 November 1921. Magda ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goebbels_children\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d31\"},\"ref\":\"d31\",\"snippet\":\" ... politics is run by families, as the recent return of the Marcos family to power sadly proves, and Gun Dealers' Daughter is the perfect novel to understand the dynastic politics that have held the Philippines in a stranglehold for decades. Soledad, our narrator and anti-hero, belongs to ... \",\"title\":\"https://electricliterature.com/9-books-about-the-complexities-of-filipino-family-bonds/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d32\"},\"ref\":\"d32\",\"snippet\":\" ... Dunn did this to set the novel up to follow two storylines: the one that Olympia (Oly), our bald-albino-hunchbacked-dwarf (!) narrator tells during her childhood and adolescence with the carnival; and the present-day story of Oly as an adult, living in a the same boarding ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/13872.Geek_Love\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d33\"},\"ref\":\"d33\",\"snippet\":\" ... feeling \\\"profoundly alone.\\\" In Small World, her sixth novel, she spins this rough outline into the mordantly funny and deeply moving account of the middle-aged Mellshman sisters, Lydia and Joyce (the narrator). Their middle sibling, Eleanor, had been born with cerebral palsy and a seizure disorder and ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.motherjones.com/media/2023/12/books-novels-best-reads-2023-daniel-schulman-ben-goldfarb-mckenzie-funk-sarah-cypher-clint-smith-matthew-desmond-safiya-sinclair/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d34\"},\"ref\":\"d34\",\"snippet\":\" ... Comics series of the same name.\\n\\nIn 2016, Davis reprised her role as Rose Maxson for the film adaptation of Fences directed by and starring Denzel Washington. Her performance garnered critical acclaim and she received her third Academy Award nomination, making her the first black actress in history ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viola_Davis\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d35\"},\"ref\":\"d35\",\"snippet\":\" ... sharp essays and state-of-the-nation novels, it's been a brilliant year for books. Here are BBC Culture's top picks.\\n\\nLiberation Day by George Saunders\\n\\nKnown as a modern master of the form, this is George Saunders' first short story collection since 2013's Tenth ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.bbc.com/culture/article/20220407-the-best-books-of-the-year-2022\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"5236e4c759fe3b31cc3eb008d850bb633b171bfd082efea8a5cb7bc94894acf6\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"b30c4d421957a2974177db3b15bf1cad50156b0bf8af9430383596941e256af1\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"second child born same day as first sibling novel narrator name\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d36\"},\"ref\":\"d36\",\"snippet\":\" ... Like Happiness\\n\\nBy Ursula Villarreal-Moura\\n\\nAn array of outlets named Ursula Villarreal-Moura's Like Happiness one of the most anticipated books of 2024, and for good reason — the novel offers a riveting perspective on gender, queerness, Latinx identity, fame, power, and more. It's 2015, and ... \",\"title\":\"https://celadonbooks.com/booklists/books-about-identity/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d37\"},\"ref\":\"d37\",\"snippet\":\" ... Applies (unsuccessfully) for Guggenheim grant with a novel concept, The Masks. First daughter Susan born. Named Best Author of Science Fiction 1949 by the National Fantasy Fan Federation. | |||||||||\\n\\n| 1950 | The Martian Chronicles published in May. Now publishing regularly in major market magazines. Receives significant review from Christopher Isherwood ... \",\"title\":\"https://liberalarts.indianapolis.iu.edu/centers/bradbury-center/ray-bradbury/timeline-of-bradburys-life/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d38\"},\"ref\":\"d38\",\"snippet\":\" ... Later that year, King was hospitalized after being hit by a van. Reflecting on the incident, he said \\\"it occurs to me that I have nearly been killed by a character out of one of my own novels. It's almost funny.\\\" He said his nurses were \\\"told ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephen_King\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d39\"},\"ref\":\"d39\",\"snippet\":\" ... novels. A crater on Mercury was named after him in 1979, and a minor planet discovered in 1981 by Lyudmila Karachkina was named 3453 Dostoevsky. Music critic and broadcaster Artemy Troitsky has hosted the radio show \\\"FM Достоевский\\\" (FM Dostoevsky) since 1997. Viewers of the TV show Name ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fyodor_Dostoevsky\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d40\"},\"ref\":\"d40\",\"snippet\":\" ... s Death Note, and adaptation of the Japanese supernatural-thriller manga of the same name. He narrated Australian documentarian Jennifer Peedom's documentary Mountain. Also that year, he co-starred as Gerhard Hardman in a film adaptation of Agatha Christie's detective novel Murder on the Orient Express ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willem_Dafoe\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d41\"},\"ref\":\"d41\",\"snippet\":\" ... A white performer named T.D.\\n\\nRice became the best known of these early minstrels.\\n\\nWearing burnt cork blackface, he danced about the stage, singing a slave song he had adapted and renamed \\\"Jump Jim Crow.\\\"\\n\\n[jaunty fiddle music] After the failure of reconstruction, African Americans would be ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.pbs.org/video/paul-laurence-dunbar-beyond-the-mask-WRjdzT/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d42\"},\"ref\":\"d42\",\"snippet\":\" ... After Christine left him, Alex later started dating again, but some of the women have either died or left him over the course of the novels. By the novel Cross, Alex discovers that an assassin named Jimmy Hats Galati, murdered his wife and was killed by his best ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alex_Cross\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d43\"},\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Dionne girls were born premature. After four months with their family, custody was signed over to the Red Cross, which paid for their care and oversaw the building of a hospital for the sisters. Less than a year after this agreement was signed, the Ontario government stepped ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dionne_quintuplets\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"235342cdf1ffb91fdd9a8581ec96428b1a2255e51b51dd43b5cd26022a36dd8f\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"9bce4f38f3e27a9b1eba1efc5f616ed670de9f43185760f91988828ab9d1d79c\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"baby named after narrator of novel born hospital renamed\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_8e1c4ab9ea89412589a9688d"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d44\"},\"ref\":\"d44\",\"snippet\":\" ... The novel's unnamed narrator, one of Stella's granddaughters, reconstructs her life history with the help of Tina and other family members. Grames picks some of her favorite novels in which the narrator isn't the main character.\\n\\nMany—maybe even most—of my favorite books are ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.publishersweekly.com/pw/by-topic/industry-news/tip-sheet/article/79938-vanishing-narrators-10-essential-books-in-which-the-narrator-isn-t-the-main-character.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_