first-person narrator, Shandy himself, sets out to write the story ... \",\"title\":\"https://readgreatliterature.com/literature-lists-timelines/restoration-and-eighteenth-century-english-literature-1660-1789/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"f07ca8f68de7cf26800de324941eeb65d96fa1e2fab32db807a424968ffa57ff\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"3484f835c0758010939a59f3276410d5b600e3546a0e13d7e1f559cdc7cff6ca\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Stella novel narrator\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d44\"},\"ref\":\"d44\",\"snippet\":\" ... The novel's unnamed narrator, one of Stella's granddaughters, reconstructs her life history with the help of Tina and other family members. Grames picks some of her favorite novels in which the narrator isn't the main character.\\n\\nMany—maybe even most—of my favorite books are ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.publishersweekly.com/pw/by-topic/industry-news/tip-sheet/article/79938-vanishing-narrators-10-essential-books-in-which-the-narrator-isn-t-the-main-character.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d45\"},\"ref\":\"d45\",\"snippet\":\" ... Snow Blind, Sons of Anarchy\\n\\nWhat's it about? This comedic novel is narrated by 15-year-old Bee, whose mother, Bernadette Fox, goes missing right before a planned family trip to Antarctica. The novel is told through emails and memos, as well as Bee's thoughts, so ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.elle.com/culture/movies-tv/g25713366/best-movies-based-on-books-2019/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d36\"},\"ref\":\"d36\",\"snippet\":\" ... The novel centers on a biracial Black man who's grappling with the unexpected loss of his teenage son when he receives word that he's inherited a former plantation from the white side of his family. Stunned by the development, the narrator travels to the property with ... \",\"title\":\"https://celadonbooks.com/booklists/books-about-identity/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d46\"},\"ref\":\"d46\",\"snippet\":\" ... Through deep personal connections to the characters we read about, we often find that we can relate to their emotional journeys — we root for them, we cry for them and we look at our own problems through the lens of a novel, becoming our own third narrator. A ... \",\"title\":\"https://fourteeneastmag.com/index.php/2020/08/07/navigating-identity-10-books-that-explore-race-culture-sexuality-and-relationships/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d47\"},\"ref\":\"d47\",\"snippet\":\" ... To start with, the novel overall is an elaborate joke about, but also a semi-serious exploration of, John Locke's theories of mind. Sterne wants to examine how people come to be who they are.\\n\\nThe first-person narrator, Shandy himself, sets out to write the story ... \",\"title\":\"https://readgreatliterature.com/literature-lists-timelines/restoration-and-eighteenth-century-english-literature-1660-1789/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"c13806a84fba1a646c66f68a74cd51fa467d45d371e82ae0cf2a3db4f60e8d3d\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"3484f835c0758